                <pb facs="1084" n="1004" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg1004"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hill to Mr. Eddy.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-09-28"><hi rendition="#italic">September 28,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hill states that Consul-General Dickinson has been instructed by telegraph
                    regarding his conduct of the matter of Miss Stone in its Bulgarian aspects, and
                    instructs that the legation equally do all in its power and discretion with the
                    Turkish Government to bring about Miss Stone’s release.</p>
                <p>Mr. Eddy is instructed, in case the agent should go to Sofia, to keep in
                    communication with him and with the mission treasurer, aiding the agent in every
                    possible discreet way.)</p>
            </div>
